      "html": "<p>Spectracanthicus zuanoni was scientifically described in early 2014. It attains a maximum length of about 15 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/finally_available_again_after_many_years_l354_en/",
      "html": "<p>L354 comes from the Rio Iriri, an affluent of the Rio Xingu.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/finally_available_again_after_many_years_l354_en/",
      "html": "<p>The scientists declare this species conspecific with L20 from the Rio Xingu. However, L20 has much smaller spots. In the same scientific paper the genus Oligancistrus was declared a synonym of Spectracanthicus.</p>"
    }
  ],
